# Paid sick leave accrual — Acme Cloud Systems (US)

> Module Sick_leave_accrual_acme
> Using Legal_types as T

Sources: SYN-005 § 4.2 (US Employee Handbook) as the base, with REAL-001
(Cal. Lab. Code § 246) and REAL-002 (C.R.S. § 8-13.3-403) as statutory floors. The
handbook itself supplies the authority for encoding the statutes as exceptions:

  SYN-005 § 4.6.1 — Where a state or local law requires a more generous rate of accrual, a
  higher accrual or use cap, a shorter waiting period, or greater carryover than this
  Section 4 provides, that law applies to employees working in that jurisdiction in place
  of the corresponding provision of this handbook.

`accrual_divisor` is the N in "one hour per every N hours worked".

```catala-metadata
declaration scope SickLeaveAccrual:
  input hours_worked content decimal
  input weeks_worked content integer
  input work_state content T.WorkState
  input days_employed content integer
  input exempt content boolean

  internal effective_hours content decimal
  internal accrual_cap content optional of decimal

  output accrual_divisor content decimal
  output accrued_hours content decimal
  output annual_use_cap content decimal
  output usable content boolean
```

## SYN-005 § 4.2.1 — the handbook's accrual rate

  Employees accrue one (1) hour of paid sick leave for every forty (40) hours worked,
  beginning on the first day of employment.

```catala
scope SickLeaveAccrual:
  label handbook_rate
  definition accrual_divisor equals 40.0

  label handbook_cap
  definition accrual_cap equals Absent
```

## SYN-005 § 4.2.2–4.2.3 — waiting period and annual use cap

  Accrued paid sick leave may be used beginning on the ninetieth (90th) calendar day of
  employment. […] An employee may use no more than forty (40) hours of paid sick leave in
  a calendar year.

```catala
scope SickLeaveAccrual:
  label handbook_waiting
  definition usable equals days_employed >= 90

  label handbook_use_cap
  definition annual_use_cap equals 40.0
```

## REAL-001, Cal. Lab. Code § 246(b)(1) — California accrual floor

  An employee shall accrue paid sick days at the rate of not less than one hour per every
  30 hours worked, beginning at the commencement of employment or the operative date of
  this article, whichever is later, subject to the use and accrual limitations set forth
  in this section.

The handbook's 1:40 is below this floor, so for California employees the statute displaces
it. § 246(j) permits an accrual cap of 80 hours and § 246(d) a use cap of 40 hours.

```catala
scope SickLeaveAccrual:
  exception handbook_rate
  definition accrual_divisor
    under condition work_state = T.WorkState.CA
    consequence equals 30.0

  exception handbook_cap
  definition accrual_cap
    under condition work_state = T.WorkState.CA
    consequence equals Present content 80.0
```

## REAL-001, Cal. Lab. Code § 246(b)(2) — exempt employees are deemed to work 40 hours

  An employee who is exempt from overtime requirements as an administrative, executive, or
  professional employee under a wage order of the Industrial Welfare Commission is deemed
  to work 40 hours per workweek for the purposes of this section.

```catala
scope SickLeaveAccrual:
  label actual_hours
  definition effective_hours equals hours_worked

  exception actual_hours
  definition effective_hours
    under condition exempt and work_state = T.WorkState.CA
    consequence equals 40.0 * (decimal of weeks_worked)
```

## REAL-002, C.R.S. § 8-13.3-403 — Colorado accrual floor and 48-hour cap

Colorado requires one hour per thirty hours worked, caps accrual and annual use at
forty-eight hours, and makes leave available as it is accrued rather than after ninety
days.

```catala
scope SickLeaveAccrual:
  exception handbook_rate
  definition accrual_divisor
    under condition work_state = T.WorkState.CO
    consequence equals 30.0

  exception handbook_cap
  definition accrual_cap
    under condition work_state = T.WorkState.CO
    consequence equals Present content 48.0

  exception handbook_use_cap
  definition annual_use_cap
    under condition work_state = T.WorkState.CO
    consequence equals 48.0

  exception handbook_waiting
  definition usable
    under condition work_state = T.WorkState.CO
    consequence equals true
```

## The accrued balance

Hours worked divided by the governing divisor, held at the governing accrual ceiling.

```catala
scope SickLeaveAccrual:
  definition accrued_hours equals
    match accrual_cap with pattern
    -- Present content ceiling:
      (if effective_hours / accrual_divisor > ceiling then ceiling
       else effective_hours / accrual_divisor)
    -- Absent: effective_hours / accrual_divisor
```
